---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="About" description="Jacob Zweig: neuroscientist by training, machine learning engineer by trade, tinkerer the rest of the time.">
  <section class="about">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm Jacob Zweig. I have a PhD in neuroscience, which I mostly use to explain how I ended
        up a machine learning engineer.
      </p>
      <p>
        I co-founded Strong Analytics and led its ML and AI work across more industries than fit
        comfortably in a sentence: sports, retail, gaming, pharma, energy, and on from there.
        These days I'm a practice lead at OneSix Solutions.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's the day job. This site is the other thing. I love to build and tinker, and it
        usually starts with something I own that almost does what I want. Lights that only talk
        to their own app. A part that doesn't exist, so it has to be printed. Then it's in pieces
        on the bench and I'm committed.
      </p>
      <p>
        I write the projects up because I learned most of this from strangers' build logs, and
        the good ones always included the boring parts: which wire was which, what the part
        actually cost, the thing they got wrong on the first try. So that's what I try to
        include. Files are free to use. If you build one, leave a comment on the project and tell
        me how it went.
      </p>
      <p>
        Code and CAD live on <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a>. New projects show up in the{' '}
        <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
